= Theorems and Proofs

#thm("Lagrange's Theorem", [
  If $G$ is a finite group and $H <= G$ a subgroup, then $|H|$ divides $|G|$.
  In particular, $|G| = [G:H] ,|H|$.
])

#cor("Order of an element")[
  For any element $g in G$ of finite order, $|g|$ divides $|G|$.
]

#proof[
  Let $n = |g|$ and let $H = chevron.l g chevron.r$ be the cyclic subgroup generated by $g$.
  Then $|H| = n$. By Lagrange’s theorem $n$ divides $|G|$.
]

#rmk[
  The converse of Lagrange’s theorem does not hold in general. For example,
  $A_4$ has order $12$ but has no subgroup of order $6$.
]
